mediate commanded openings are not supported. Dimensions omitted from move_to are filled from the measured end-effector state by the tool layer.\n\nThe tool layer interpolates targets under its shared motion limits. The robot may not reach a target before the next observation; use the measured state and images to determine what happened. No additional settling motion is inserted after a tool call.\n\nState fields: eef_pos is the measured end-effector position; eef_quat uses (w,x,y,z); eef_yaw is in radians; gripper is measured normalized opening; eef_state is [x,y,z,yaw,gripper]. joint_pos and joint_vel describe the seven arm joints in radians and radians per second. joint_eff contains arm actuator torques in N m, including controller compensation; it is not a fingertip contact sensor.\n\nCameras: front and side are fixed views; wrist moves with the hand. All are 224x224 RGB images with the top row at the top of the view. The wrist view can rotate as the hand rotates. No fixed mapping from image directions to world x/y is assumed. Each request includes the current three views and retains images from at most the two most recent observations.",
